<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada buys Canada dollars again - traders.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada buys Canada dollars again - traders.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada intervened and bought Canadian dollars for U.S. dollars a second time on Tuesday as the currency traded around the C$1.3843 level.</p>
<p>Dealers said intervention was direct through banks and considered heavy as the currency weakened through key support.</p>
<p>Following the intervention, the Canadian dollar was trading at C$1.3840 after opening at C$1.3766 and Monday's close of C$1.3765. Traders expect further losses.</p>
<p>The Bank of Canada does not comment on intervention.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
